WEBVTT

00:08.258 --> 00:11.261
[♪ pensive theme music playing]

01:07.901 --> 01:09.903
[♪ theme concludes]

01:13.323 --> 01:15.909
-[rain falling]
-[radio beeps]

01:15.950 --> 01:17.202
[Shauna] [on radio]
Jimmy K.

01:17.243 --> 01:18.578
-[thunder rumbling]
-[Dina exclaiming]

01:18.620 --> 01:20.497
[Jimmy] [over radio]
Yeah, go for Jimmy K.

01:20.497 --> 01:22.499
[Shauna] Tell your division
we're going silent,
Isaac's orders.

01:22.499 --> 01:24.209
-Call your boats back.
Radio silent.
-[Dina] Pull it out!

01:24.250 --> 01:25.710
I swear to God,
if you don't do it, I will.

01:25.752 --> 01:28.545
-[Jesse] I said maybe.
-[Jimmy] Alright, copy.

01:28.588 --> 01:31.382
-[Jesse] This is gonna hurt.
-It already fucking hurts!

01:31.424 --> 01:33.926
[Dina screaming, wailing]

01:33.968 --> 01:35.095
[thunder crashing]

01:36.387 --> 01:39.057
[panting]
Jesse, don't let me...

01:39.098 --> 01:40.683
You can't let me die.

01:40.683 --> 01:42.393
-Yeah, I know.
-No, you don't.

01:42.435 --> 01:44.062
Listen, if I pull it,
it's gonna tear an artery.

01:44.104 --> 01:45.854
-I need to push it through.
-How do you know that?

01:45.896 --> 01:47.857
-What if it's the wrong way?
-I know where the arteries are.

01:47.857 --> 01:49.692
-No, you don't,
you're not a doctor!
-Dina, shut up!

01:49.692 --> 01:51.527
[thunder rumbling]

01:51.569 --> 01:53.571
[breathing heavily]

01:54.572 --> 01:55.865
Hey.

01:55.907 --> 01:56.908
Dina.

01:58.785 --> 02:00.745
I got you, alright?

02:00.787 --> 02:01.996
I got you.

02:03.414 --> 02:05.416
[Dina sobbing]

02:08.336 --> 02:10.713
-[wailing]
-I know, I know.

02:10.755 --> 02:12.715
I know.
Have some, okay?

02:12.715 --> 02:14.217
-No.
-It's gonna help.
Have some.

02:14.259 --> 02:15.593
I said no.

02:16.302 --> 02:18.304
[thunder continues]

02:22.892 --> 02:24.144
[Jesse] Okay.

02:24.185 --> 02:26.563
[breathing heavily]

02:26.563 --> 02:28.064
[groaning loudly]
Just do it.

02:28.106 --> 02:29.190
[Dina screaming]

02:35.155 --> 02:37.156
[rain pattering]

02:38.908 --> 02:40.910
[thunder rumbling]

02:50.962 --> 02:52.422
[loud banging]

02:52.463 --> 02:54.132
[Ellie] It's me.

02:54.174 --> 02:56.091
-[banging]
-Jesse! Dina!

02:56.091 --> 02:57.760
What's the name
of your horse?

02:57.760 --> 02:59.971
[Ellie]
Shimmer. I'm alone.
Open the fucking door!

03:01.764 --> 03:03.766
[heavy rain falling]

03:06.311 --> 03:08.478
[items clattering inside]

03:10.773 --> 03:12.734
-Where is she?
-What happened to you?

03:13.902 --> 03:16.321
Dina? Is she--

03:16.362 --> 03:17.947
She's okay.
She's in the dressing room.

03:17.989 --> 03:20.658
-[whispering] Dressing room.
-Ellie, where were you?

03:22.619 --> 03:24.621
[electricity buzzing softly]

03:31.002 --> 03:33.004
[footsteps approaching]

03:34.505 --> 03:35.506
[door creaking]

03:36.090 --> 03:38.091
[Dina softly snoring]

03:41.387 --> 03:42.889
[door closes]

03:47.977 --> 03:51.439
[♪ gentle music playing]

04:00.073 --> 04:01.074
[Ellie sighs]

04:17.632 --> 04:19.050
Hi.

04:22.470 --> 04:23.721
Let me see.

04:45.743 --> 04:47.578
Is the baby...?

04:49.497 --> 04:51.541
-It's okay.
-How do you know?

04:52.792 --> 04:54.294
I just do.

04:57.380 --> 04:58.673
[sighs deeply]

05:11.561 --> 05:13.187
Sit over there.

05:14.188 --> 05:15.189
Alright.

05:21.696 --> 05:24.574
[exhales sharply]
Shirt off.

05:31.164 --> 05:33.166
[wincing]

05:33.207 --> 05:35.752
-Okay, arms up.
-[grunting]

05:35.793 --> 05:38.379
[Dina]
Three, two, one.

05:39.464 --> 05:40.757
[grunting]

05:41.883 --> 05:43.885
[Ellie sighs]

05:53.811 --> 05:55.813
[water sloshing]

06:04.030 --> 06:05.615
[Ellie wincing]

06:08.117 --> 06:09.952
So, are you gonna tell me
what happened?

06:14.374 --> 06:15.583
[Ellie] I found her.

06:17.251 --> 06:18.628
I found Nora.

06:20.963 --> 06:21.964
Good.

06:23.633 --> 06:24.967
Does she know
where Abby is?

06:25.510 --> 06:28.513
Yes, but she only
said two words.

06:29.680 --> 06:31.641
"Whale," and then "wheel."

06:33.183 --> 06:36.396
-What does that mean?
-I don't know. Maybe nothing.

06:37.146 --> 06:39.148
She was infected,
it was already setting in.

06:45.488 --> 06:46.864
Hm.

06:48.324 --> 06:50.827
-[water splashing]
-[Dina sighs]

06:55.373 --> 06:57.082
[whispering]
I made her talk.

07:02.171 --> 07:04.632
I thought it would be
harder to do.

07:06.509 --> 07:08.428
But it wasn't.

07:09.846 --> 07:11.431
It was easy.

07:13.641 --> 07:15.726
I just kept hurting her.

07:21.941 --> 07:23.276
Did you kill her?

07:24.193 --> 07:25.194
[Ellie] No.

07:26.487 --> 07:27.697
I left her.

07:30.908 --> 07:33.661
Yeah, well, maybe she got
what she deserved.

07:34.871 --> 07:36.873
[water sloshing]

07:39.250 --> 07:40.835
[Ellie] [whispering]
Maybe she didn't.

07:52.680 --> 07:55.683
[♪ gentle, solemn music playing]

08:13.242 --> 08:14.994
It was a long time ago.

08:17.497 --> 08:19.207
Before I came to Jackson.

08:23.294 --> 08:26.756
There was a Firefly base
in Salt Lake City.

08:26.756 --> 08:28.424
They had a hospital there.

08:28.424 --> 08:30.676
They were gonna use me
to make a cure.

08:33.011 --> 08:34.889
But it meant that
I would have died.

08:36.807 --> 08:39.727
And Joel found out.

08:46.776 --> 08:49.987
And he killed everyone
in the hospital.

08:51.989 --> 08:53.491
Everyone.

08:55.743 --> 08:57.870
He killed Abby's father.

09:00.206 --> 09:03.918
He was a doctor,
and Joel shot him in the head.

09:06.087 --> 09:07.588
To save me.

09:08.464 --> 09:10.466
[Ellie breathing shakily]

09:15.096 --> 09:17.056
So, that's why they came.

09:20.685 --> 09:21.978
[Ellie sniffles]

09:23.062 --> 09:24.647
Did you know
who they were?

09:26.023 --> 09:27.024
[swallowing hard]

09:32.780 --> 09:34.574
But I knew what he did.

09:40.538 --> 09:41.998
I'm sorry.

09:51.882 --> 09:53.467
We need to go home.

09:55.928 --> 09:57.930
[Dina grunting softly]

10:11.068 --> 10:13.070
-[birdsong]
-[water dripping]

10:35.760 --> 10:37.762
-[walkie clicking on]
-[radio static]

10:48.898 --> 10:50.650
Do you have any extra
nine-millimeter?

10:55.655 --> 10:56.781
Thanks.

11:04.622 --> 11:06.624
[door opens]

11:11.379 --> 11:13.589
You shouldn't be
on your feet yet.

11:13.631 --> 11:15.216
I'll go back to the couch
in a second.

11:16.258 --> 11:17.551
I promise.

11:19.762 --> 11:21.138
Give me your wrist.

11:25.393 --> 11:27.061
The other one.

11:44.912 --> 11:46.205
It's for good luck.

11:47.415 --> 11:49.417
Not sure
it's been working for you.

11:50.334 --> 11:51.627
I'm alive.

11:53.212 --> 11:55.631
I can do this alone,
if you want Ellie to stay.

11:55.631 --> 11:56.799
No.

12:00.219 --> 12:02.638
-[bag zipping]
-We'll be safer together.

12:03.556 --> 12:05.641
Our rendezvous
point's not far.

12:05.683 --> 12:07.810
Assuming Tommy's there,
we should be back

12:07.810 --> 12:10.146
-well before sundown.
-Okay, good.

12:11.313 --> 12:13.357
You okay to barricade?

12:13.399 --> 12:15.568
Yeah. Go.

12:15.609 --> 12:16.610
Yeah.

12:20.406 --> 12:22.408
[footsteps receding]

12:24.493 --> 12:26.495
[scraping, thudding]

12:36.922 --> 12:38.507
[door closes]

12:53.189 --> 12:55.733
-Where's the rendezvous?
-The bookstore.

13:00.029 --> 13:01.781
You ever gonna tell me
how you found the theater?

13:03.032 --> 13:05.284
You ever gonna tell me what
happened to you last night?

13:09.205 --> 13:11.373
We followed the likeliest
path into the city.

13:11.415 --> 13:13.542
Found the place
you stashed Shimmer.

13:13.542 --> 13:16.128
She's still there doing alright.
Not that you asked.

13:16.170 --> 13:18.798
And then,
we saw the WLF sign
on the TV station,

13:18.839 --> 13:21.592
figured that's where you went,
split up a two-square-mile area

13:21.634 --> 13:23.219
around it and began searching.

13:23.219 --> 13:24.845
That's how
I found the theater.

13:26.055 --> 13:27.515
Oh, you make it sound easy.

13:28.557 --> 13:31.977
It took two days
and a lot of close calls.

13:35.272 --> 13:36.398
Thank you.

13:37.691 --> 13:39.235
I mean it, honestly.

13:41.070 --> 13:42.571
Look, I know you're angry--

13:42.571 --> 13:44.740
Last night,
Dina said, "I can't die."

13:44.740 --> 13:48.077
Not, "I don't want to die."
"I can't."

13:48.077 --> 13:50.746
And then I offered her whiskey,
and she refused.

13:50.788 --> 13:52.581
Dina, the girl
who's never turned down

13:52.581 --> 13:54.165
a free drink in her life,

13:54.208 --> 13:56.335
seconds before
I was gonna push
a crossbow bolt

13:56.377 --> 13:57.962
-through her leg.
-That's weird.

13:58.003 --> 14:00.089
-I don't know why she--
-Yes, you do.

14:00.089 --> 14:02.424
I'm not stupid
and I'm not blind.

14:02.424 --> 14:04.635
Ellie, I see the way you two
look at each other.

14:05.344 --> 14:06.846
It's different now.

14:08.097 --> 14:11.767
Yeah, and I bet
she even tells you things
she wouldn't tell me.

14:11.809 --> 14:13.310
Like how she's pregnant.

14:16.522 --> 14:17.606
Fuck.

14:18.107 --> 14:19.066
[Jesse exhales sharply]

14:21.235 --> 14:22.987
Oh, shit, you were guessing?

14:24.029 --> 14:25.072
Oh, God.

14:29.034 --> 14:31.829
Look, she's obviously
gonna tell you.

14:31.871 --> 14:35.290
So, just act surprised, okay?

14:35.332 --> 14:37.501
None of this has to change
things between us.

14:37.543 --> 14:39.712
Everything changing
doesn't have to change things?

14:40.754 --> 14:43.132
Well, how 'bout this
for something new?

14:43.132 --> 14:46.677
I'm gonna be a father,
which means I can't die.

14:46.719 --> 14:48.804
But because of you,
we're stuck in a war zone.

14:48.846 --> 14:50.890
So, how 'bout we skip
the apologies

14:50.931 --> 14:53.309
and just go find Tommy
so I can get us and my kid

14:53.350 --> 14:54.560
the fuck outta Seattle?

15:01.609 --> 15:04.612
[♪ dramatic music playing]

15:17.249 --> 15:19.043
There's more
than one of her?

15:19.084 --> 15:21.003
[Jesse] I guess so.
I don't know.

15:21.045 --> 15:22.838
[thunder rumbling]

15:22.838 --> 15:24.632
We need to move faster.

15:28.802 --> 15:31.472
[thunder crashing]

15:36.769 --> 15:39.897
-[rain pattering]
-[both panting]

15:43.734 --> 15:45.945
Please tell me we're close.

15:45.986 --> 15:48.113
[exhales sharply]
Think we have two more blocks.

15:49.365 --> 15:51.450
Let's give it a minute,
see if it dies down,

15:51.492 --> 15:53.035
-and then we'll--
-[gunshot]

15:53.077 --> 15:54.787
-Shit.
-Go.

15:54.828 --> 15:56.622
-[soldier 1] I see him!
-[soldier 2]
You're fucking dead, Scar!

15:56.664 --> 15:58.040
-[gunshot]
-Nowhere to run!

15:58.082 --> 15:59.917
[Jesse]
There, there, there.
Go! Get down!

15:59.959 --> 16:02.086
-[gunshot]
-[soldier 2] He's heading off
in the garage, keep going!

16:03.671 --> 16:05.381
-Get on the ground!
-[Seraphite panting]

16:05.422 --> 16:06.590
You piece of shit!

16:08.008 --> 16:09.635
[Seraphite] [chanting]
The world is not in balance,

16:09.677 --> 16:10.803
but I've done my part
to right it.

16:10.844 --> 16:12.304
[soldier 2]
How'd you get past our line?

16:12.721 --> 16:14.765
-[Seraphite continues chanting]
-How?!

16:14.807 --> 16:16.225
The world is not in balance.

16:16.225 --> 16:17.893
But I have done
my part to right it.

16:17.893 --> 16:19.353
[crying] She has led me
through the storm.

16:19.395 --> 16:20.562
Now I must rest.

16:20.562 --> 16:21.814
-May she guide me.
-I'm sorry, what?

16:21.855 --> 16:22.898
May she guide me.
May she guide me.

16:22.898 --> 16:24.066
-[punch thuds]
-[Seraphite screams]

16:24.066 --> 16:25.776
[Burton]
Get his clothes off.

16:25.818 --> 16:26.902
[Seraphite] No! No!

16:27.736 --> 16:29.071
Wait! Wait! No!

16:29.113 --> 16:30.656
Stop it!
Get off of me!

16:31.323 --> 16:33.409
-[Seraphite] Stop!
-[soldier] Come on,
you little piece of shit!

16:33.409 --> 16:34.910
-[Burton] Drag him.
-[soldier] Fucking go!

16:34.952 --> 16:36.996
-[Seraphite screaming]
-Let's fucking go!

16:38.247 --> 16:41.290
-[Seraphite continues yelling]
-[Burton] Let's go! Go!

16:42.126 --> 16:45.129
[♪ tense music playing]

16:47.006 --> 16:49.383
-Get the fuck off!
-Ellie.

16:50.426 --> 16:51.427
Ellie.

16:52.928 --> 16:54.430
-Ellie!
-What?!

16:54.430 --> 16:56.098
There are six of them
and two of us.

16:56.098 --> 16:58.017
-What do you think
would've happened?
-He's a fucking kid!

16:58.058 --> 17:00.436
Ellie, these people
are shooting each other,

17:00.436 --> 17:02.604
lynching each other,
ripping each other's guts out.

17:02.646 --> 17:04.440
Even the kids.

17:04.481 --> 17:06.525
I am not dying out here.

17:06.942 --> 17:09.611
[panting]
Not for any of them.

17:09.611 --> 17:12.321
This is not our war.

17:17.243 --> 17:18.369
Let's go.

17:25.210 --> 17:28.213
-[thunder crashing]
-[people shouting]

17:31.800 --> 17:34.178
[soldier]
Can't leave it there.
You gotta move your truck.

17:34.887 --> 17:36.930
[intense rain falling]

17:38.140 --> 17:40.684
[soldiers shouting]

17:41.602 --> 17:43.979
[thunder continues rumbling]

17:44.021 --> 17:45.981
[Park]
Good news.

17:45.981 --> 17:48.859
Melissa and Kristi are saying
the storm's a convergence zone.

17:48.901 --> 17:50.110
Mm-hmm.

17:52.946 --> 17:54.323
It's gonna get even bigger.

17:56.325 --> 17:59.203
Orders have been relayed
verbally, everything's set.

18:01.538 --> 18:04.083
-[soldiers shouting in distance]
-[thunder rumbling]

18:04.124 --> 18:05.918
All the officers are on board,

18:05.959 --> 18:08.420
but I think the rank and file
are a little scared.

18:08.462 --> 18:10.089
Aren't you?

18:12.549 --> 18:15.761
It'll be dark by 21:30.

18:15.803 --> 18:17.971
-We'll start the staggered
load in--
-Any word on Abby?

18:20.891 --> 18:22.768
Not since yesterday.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.729
And we still
haven't found Owen.

18:29.149 --> 18:30.567
Mel is missing now, too.

18:31.985 --> 18:34.988
So, her entire crew
just disappears,

18:35.030 --> 18:36.406
tonight of all nights?

18:39.785 --> 18:41.203
We still have Manny.

18:41.203 --> 18:43.205
Well, we have a lot
of Mannys, don't we?

18:43.205 --> 18:44.957
And enough Owens and Mels.

18:46.083 --> 18:47.668
But only one Abby.

18:50.587 --> 18:52.047
Okay, what the fuck?

18:52.089 --> 18:54.591
She's a good soldier.
Great, even.

18:54.633 --> 18:56.718
But we have an entire
fuckin' army out there,

18:56.760 --> 18:58.554
and you're acting like
she's the most important.

18:59.596 --> 19:01.640
What-- [scoffs]

19:01.682 --> 19:03.058
You in love with her
or something?

19:03.100 --> 19:04.518
[laughing]

19:04.560 --> 19:07.479
[Park scoffs]
I mean, I don't know.

19:07.521 --> 19:09.314
You wouldn't be
the first old man to--

19:09.356 --> 19:11.567
Okay, okay. No.

19:12.401 --> 19:14.862
[rain pattering loudly]

19:23.871 --> 19:25.873
[thunder continues rumbling]

19:27.207 --> 19:29.084
By the time the sun
comes up tomorrow,

19:29.126 --> 19:31.336
there's a very good chance
you'll be dead.

19:32.921 --> 19:34.965
There's an even better
chance I'll be dead.

19:36.592 --> 19:39.469
So then, what happens to that
entire fucking army out there,

19:39.511 --> 19:42.181
who despite their badass name,
are very much sheep?

19:43.849 --> 19:45.267
Who leads them?

19:46.560 --> 19:48.020
Who secures our future?

19:50.522 --> 19:52.191
It was supposed to be her.

20:00.157 --> 20:01.992
Well, she's fucked off,
Isaac.

20:05.120 --> 20:06.371
So, maybe it wasn't.

20:18.675 --> 20:21.720
[thunder crashing]

20:26.725 --> 20:27.809
[Jesse] Fuck.

20:30.437 --> 20:31.813
Is that your shit?

20:31.813 --> 20:33.482
Yeah.

20:33.523 --> 20:35.484
[Ellie] Alright.
So, if he's not here...

20:35.484 --> 20:37.402
[Jesse]
It's gonna be fine.
He'll make it back.

20:37.444 --> 20:40.155
-Well, what if he's in trouble?
-"What if"?

20:40.155 --> 20:42.366
He is in trouble.
We're all in trouble.

20:42.407 --> 20:44.409
[thunder continues]

20:45.953 --> 20:47.829
Here we are again.

20:47.829 --> 20:49.748
You and me
in bad fuckin' weather.

20:55.837 --> 20:57.839
[intense rain pattering]

20:59.633 --> 21:02.636
[♪ gentle guitar music playing]

21:29.037 --> 21:30.455
[Jesse]
You picked a good one.

21:31.832 --> 21:33.375
I should have
thought of that.

21:37.087 --> 21:40.424
Listen, about me and her,
I don't really know what to say.

21:44.261 --> 21:46.054
Right now,
we got a lot of problems.

21:46.096 --> 21:48.390
Like a wounded pregnant girl.

21:48.390 --> 21:50.559
Maybe Tommy's dead.
Maybe we'll be dead.

21:50.559 --> 21:54.187
So, let me at least just
get this one off the table.

21:56.648 --> 21:58.442
Yes, I love her.

22:00.235 --> 22:01.737
But not the way you do.

22:06.867 --> 22:08.243
[sighs]

22:11.163 --> 22:13.498
Remember that group
that stopped by Jackson

22:13.540 --> 22:16.418
for a few weeks on their way
south to Mexico?

22:16.460 --> 22:18.420
Uh, from Alberta?

22:18.420 --> 22:21.006
Yeah, they had some
decent shit to trade.

22:21.048 --> 22:23.425
There was this girl with them.

22:23.425 --> 22:24.968
She was a couple years
older than me.

22:25.010 --> 22:27.929
I don't know if you remember.
She was selling paintings,

22:27.929 --> 22:29.848
like landscapes and shit.

22:29.890 --> 22:32.434
-Were they good?
-No.

22:33.643 --> 22:35.312
I bought four of 'em.
[chuckles]

22:38.732 --> 22:40.442
That fuckin' feeling...

22:41.485 --> 22:45.030
when you're falling for someone
and they're falling right back.

22:46.114 --> 22:47.115
Hm.

22:51.161 --> 22:54.456
-So, what happened?
-Best two weeks of my life.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.958
But she couldn't stay.

22:56.958 --> 22:59.044
Didn't want to abandon
her family like that.

23:00.170 --> 23:02.506
So, she asked me
to go with them instead.

23:04.716 --> 23:06.051
And I wanted to.

23:07.636 --> 23:08.929
More than anything.

23:10.180 --> 23:11.765
Then, why didn't you?

23:14.309 --> 23:16.812
Because the people of Jackson
took me in, raised me,

23:16.853 --> 23:19.231
cared for me,
because everyone there

23:19.272 --> 23:21.942
is counting on me
to be the next Maria.

23:23.735 --> 23:27.989
Because I was taught
to put other people first.

23:30.283 --> 23:32.327
Okay.

23:33.328 --> 23:36.706
Got it. So, you're
Saint Jesse of Wyoming

23:36.748 --> 23:38.875
and everyone else
is a fucking asshole.

23:38.917 --> 23:40.502
You can make fun
of me all you want,

23:40.502 --> 23:42.671
but let me
ask you this, Ellie.

23:42.712 --> 23:46.091
I go with that girl to Mexico,
who saves your ass in Seattle?

23:48.885 --> 23:50.345
[soldier] [on radio]
Under fire! I repeat!

23:50.387 --> 23:53.682
We are under fire.
Under fire, Southlake Marina.

23:53.682 --> 23:55.725
-Sniper, not a Scar!
-[gunshot over radio]

23:55.767 --> 23:56.768
-Unidentified--
-[gunshot]

23:56.810 --> 23:58.603
Goddammit!

23:58.645 --> 24:00.564
Two of us pinned down.
We need backup!

24:00.605 --> 24:02.232
-[soldier 2] No radios. Repeat.
-Sniper.

24:02.274 --> 24:03.775
-No radios.
-It's gotta be Tommy.

24:03.817 --> 24:06.403
[indistinct radio chatter]

24:06.445 --> 24:08.363
This is South Lake.
There's two piers right here.

24:09.281 --> 24:10.532
It's gotta be one of them.

24:10.532 --> 24:12.325
Alright, pack your shit.
We're going up.

24:14.911 --> 24:17.914
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

24:20.292 --> 24:21.668
[door opens]

24:26.089 --> 24:27.257
[door closes]

24:40.979 --> 24:41.980
[distant gunshot]

24:44.065 --> 24:46.318
-[gunshot]
-You hear that?

24:47.110 --> 24:48.361
It's in the right direction.

24:49.988 --> 24:53.074
I don't see an easy way north,
but if he got there,

24:53.074 --> 24:54.659
it means we can, too.

24:55.660 --> 24:57.078
Ellie.

24:57.078 --> 24:58.413
[whispering]
The wheel.

24:58.455 --> 25:00.248
-The whale.
-What?

25:00.248 --> 25:02.250
-She's in the fucking aquarium.
-Who?

25:02.292 --> 25:04.753
Abby, the one who killed Joel.
She's in the aquarium.

25:04.794 --> 25:06.129
It's too far to swim.
We need a boat.

25:06.171 --> 25:08.507
-What are you talking about?
-What?

25:08.548 --> 25:10.842
No, Tommy's over there.
That's where we're going.

25:12.844 --> 25:14.846
[gunshots continue]

25:14.888 --> 25:16.973
You don't know that's him.

25:17.933 --> 25:19.476
-Yes, we do.
-We don't.

25:19.518 --> 25:21.436
And even if it is,
he's got them pinned down.

25:21.436 --> 25:23.021
For now.
They called for backup.

25:23.063 --> 25:25.273
Then, he'll pin
more of them down.
I know him.

25:25.315 --> 25:27.943
-He would want me to do this.
-[gunshots continue]

25:27.943 --> 25:30.445
And Jesus Christ,
if three more people
had voted with you,

25:30.445 --> 25:32.948
-you'd be coming with me.
-[thunder rumbling]

25:35.534 --> 25:37.702
[breathing heavily]
I voted no.

25:41.706 --> 25:43.458
Why?

25:43.458 --> 25:46.127
Because everything you do,
you do for you.

25:46.127 --> 25:47.963
Oh, my God.

25:48.004 --> 25:49.631
-Ellie.
-Oh, my God.

25:49.631 --> 25:52.300
Ellie, it wasn't
in the best interest
of the community.

25:52.342 --> 25:54.302
Fuck the community!

25:54.344 --> 25:56.471
All you do is talk about
the fucking community.

25:56.513 --> 25:57.681
You hypocrite.

25:57.722 --> 25:59.516
You think you're good
and I'm bad?

26:00.809 --> 26:03.478
You let a kid die today,
Jesse.

26:03.520 --> 26:06.314
Because why?
He wasn't in your community?

26:07.774 --> 26:09.526
Let me tell you
about my community.

26:10.902 --> 26:13.488
My community was beaten
to death in front of me

26:13.530 --> 26:15.657
while I was forced
to fucking watch.

26:15.699 --> 26:18.034
So, don't look at me
like you're better than me

26:18.076 --> 26:19.494
or like you'd do
anything differently

26:19.494 --> 26:21.830
if you were in my shoes,
because you're not,

26:21.830 --> 26:23.081
and you wouldn't.

26:23.123 --> 26:24.833
[gunshots continue]

26:25.250 --> 26:27.252
[heavy rain continues]

26:29.838 --> 26:31.339
I really hope you make it.

26:33.466 --> 26:36.469
[♪ dramatic music playing]

26:38.471 --> 26:40.056
[distant gunshot]

26:45.228 --> 26:47.230
[thunder rumbling]

26:48.398 --> 26:51.401
[♪ dramatic music
continues playing]

26:54.571 --> 26:55.572
[thunder crashing]

27:08.835 --> 27:10.837
-[thunder rumbling]
-[metal squeaking]

27:21.806 --> 27:23.808
[breathing heavily]

27:29.606 --> 27:31.608
[thunder continues rumbling]

27:38.531 --> 27:39.991
[WLF guard]
Hey, let's move, come on.

27:40.784 --> 27:42.077
Come on, we gotta
meet 'em out there.

27:43.244 --> 27:45.580
[guards continue
chatting indistinctly]

28:02.889 --> 28:05.892
[♪ tense music playing]

28:08.937 --> 28:11.981
[motors revving]

28:21.282 --> 28:22.367
Load 'em up.

28:23.576 --> 28:24.577
Let's go!

28:31.418 --> 28:32.961
Last one's on board.

28:39.217 --> 28:41.219
[thunder rumbling]

28:47.142 --> 28:50.353
[boat motors rumbling]

29:05.827 --> 29:07.829
[thunder crashing]

29:17.630 --> 29:19.674
[grunting]

29:19.716 --> 29:21.718
[motor revving]

30:08.556 --> 30:09.933
[grunting]

30:15.146 --> 30:16.147
[shouting]

30:16.981 --> 30:18.483
[wave crashing]

30:20.360 --> 30:22.362
[thunder crashing]

30:34.541 --> 30:36.584
[water lapping]

30:36.584 --> 30:38.586
[Ellie gasping]

30:41.673 --> 30:43.716
[Ellie coughing]

30:45.176 --> 30:46.928
[grunting]

30:49.097 --> 30:50.682
[continues coughing]

30:54.811 --> 30:56.813
[thunder crashing]

30:58.773 --> 31:01.776
[♪ dramatic music playing]

31:06.281 --> 31:08.032
[distant whistling]

31:08.074 --> 31:10.076
[Ellie gasping]

31:17.917 --> 31:19.919
[grunting]

31:22.422 --> 31:24.591
[Ellie exclaiming]

31:27.176 --> 31:29.178
[distant whistling]

31:43.651 --> 31:44.944
[gasping]

31:47.155 --> 31:49.157
-[Ellie shouting]
-[Seraphites grunting]

31:54.037 --> 31:56.039
[Ellie continues shouting]

32:01.878 --> 32:03.379
[Ellie whimpering]

32:04.881 --> 32:06.215
[thunder crashing]

32:06.257 --> 32:09.761
No! I'm not from here!
I'm not a Wolf!

32:09.802 --> 32:11.512
Tell them.

32:17.769 --> 32:19.520
[gasping]

32:19.520 --> 32:21.522
[grunting, struggling]

32:23.650 --> 32:25.068
[choking]

32:28.071 --> 32:30.073
[gasping, choking continue]

32:37.872 --> 32:40.708
[horn bellowing]

32:40.750 --> 32:43.086
The village.
The village!

32:43.127 --> 32:45.088
[Ellie gasping]

32:45.922 --> 32:46.965
Leave her!

32:47.256 --> 32:48.299
[Ellie yelps]

32:53.972 --> 32:55.974
[gasping]

33:06.985 --> 33:08.820
[thunder rumbling]

33:14.659 --> 33:16.661
[grunting]

33:21.040 --> 33:23.042
[motor revving]

33:26.838 --> 33:29.173
[breathing heavily]

33:32.218 --> 33:34.220
[distant explosion booming]

33:49.569 --> 33:51.571
[thunder crashing]

34:02.665 --> 34:04.000
[grunting]

34:11.215 --> 34:14.217
[♪ dramatic music playing]

34:22.893 --> 34:24.896
[thunder rumbling]

34:32.070 --> 34:33.071
[grunting]

34:46.501 --> 34:48.460
[waves crashing]

34:50.670 --> 34:52.422
[thunder continues rumbling]

34:52.465 --> 34:54.467
[water dripping]

35:11.192 --> 35:12.235
[thudding]

35:18.074 --> 35:22.328
[♪ dramatic music
continues playing]

35:45.226 --> 35:48.396
[♪ ominous music playing]

36:03.953 --> 36:05.955
[water dripping]

36:13.379 --> 36:16.382
[breathing heavily]

36:33.941 --> 36:35.943
[thunder rumbling]

36:54.629 --> 36:55.922
[thunder crashing]

37:02.345 --> 37:05.348
[♪ tense music playing]

37:18.653 --> 37:20.655
[indistinct chatter]

37:21.614 --> 37:22.907
[Mel]
...for her, so don't
make me sound like

37:22.949 --> 37:25.576
I'm being some
kind of heartless bitch.

37:25.618 --> 37:27.662
I'm not.
And let's be honest,

37:27.662 --> 37:29.705
this isn't about them
anyways, Owen.

37:29.747 --> 37:31.666
You're talking about being
behind enemy lines

37:31.707 --> 37:33.084
alone at night.

37:33.125 --> 37:34.877
This is suicide
under normal circumstances,

37:34.919 --> 37:36.504
and you want to do this now?

37:36.504 --> 37:38.089
Do you even understand
what's going on?

37:38.130 --> 37:39.215
[Owen]
I understand everything,

37:39.257 --> 37:40.925
but I don't have
a choice, do I?

37:40.967 --> 37:42.843
It's Abby.

37:42.843 --> 37:45.680
Of course, you have a choice.
And so do I.

37:45.721 --> 37:48.516
And I am choosing no,
also because it's Abby.

37:48.557 --> 37:50.601
Fine, I'll do it on my own,
like always.

37:50.643 --> 37:52.353
I can make it
there and back in 30.

37:52.395 --> 37:53.771
If you're still here,
you can get on board

37:53.813 --> 37:56.065
and keep going with us.
If you're not, you're not.

37:57.108 --> 37:59.193
Fuck you, Owen.

37:59.235 --> 38:00.403
[Ellie] Hands up.

38:04.740 --> 38:07.702
-Where's Abby?
-You gotta be kidding me.

38:07.702 --> 38:09.453
Okay. Easy.

38:13.749 --> 38:15.543
I'm the one
who kept you alive, right?

38:16.711 --> 38:19.046
[breathing heavily]

38:19.046 --> 38:20.214
[gun cocking]

38:22.174 --> 38:23.718
We don't know where she is.

38:23.718 --> 38:26.595
You were just talking about her,
so, yes, you fucking do.

38:32.184 --> 38:33.561
You, bring me that map.

38:34.478 --> 38:37.064
You're gonna point
to where Abby is,

38:37.106 --> 38:40.568
and then you're gonna do it,
and it better fucking match.

38:45.781 --> 38:47.450
You have five seconds.

38:48.951 --> 38:51.078
-Four.
-She's gonna kill us
either way.

38:51.120 --> 38:52.204
[Ellie] No, I won't.

38:53.914 --> 38:55.624
Because I'm not like you.

38:57.668 --> 38:58.669
Three.

39:01.714 --> 39:02.715
Two.

39:04.133 --> 39:06.761
I-- I'll do it.
I'll do it.

39:07.928 --> 39:09.096
I'll show you.

39:10.973 --> 39:12.308
Slowly.

39:14.060 --> 39:15.853
S-Slowly.

39:15.895 --> 39:19.482
[♪ tense music playing]

39:29.784 --> 39:30.826
[gunshots]

39:34.330 --> 39:35.664
[Mel] Oh, God.

39:42.797 --> 39:45.007
Oh, God. Oh...

39:45.049 --> 39:46.967
[body thuds]

39:46.967 --> 39:48.636
[groaning]

39:48.636 --> 39:51.305
Knife? [gasps]
Do you have a knife?

39:53.349 --> 39:55.476
I have, like, 30 seconds.
Get the fuck over here, please.

39:55.518 --> 39:57.937
Please, please, please.

39:59.772 --> 40:02.358
-Knife. Knife.
-[switchblade clicking]

40:02.400 --> 40:05.861
You're gonna take it out.
You're gonna get it out.

40:06.779 --> 40:07.780
What?

40:09.907 --> 40:12.326
-I don't know how to do that.
-I do. I do.

40:12.993 --> 40:15.162
One incision.
That's all it is.

40:15.162 --> 40:17.456
And then, be sure
to tie the cord.

40:18.916 --> 40:21.210
Work fast.
Work fast.

40:21.252 --> 40:24.046
[labored breathing]
Work fast.

40:24.088 --> 40:26.465
-Work fast. Very fast.
-Okay. Okay.

40:30.302 --> 40:31.554
How deep?

40:31.595 --> 40:33.889
-Deeper than you think.
-Which way?

40:35.599 --> 40:36.684
Which way?

40:39.103 --> 40:41.689
Low transverse.
Transverse.

40:41.689 --> 40:44.191
What?
I don't know what that means.

40:44.233 --> 40:45.526
Low transverse.

40:46.777 --> 40:48.529
Low transverse.

40:48.571 --> 40:51.615
What?
Tell me what that means.

40:53.367 --> 40:55.786
[weakly] You're doing good.
You're doing really good.

40:59.206 --> 41:00.374
Is it out?

41:03.377 --> 41:04.587
Is it out?

41:22.897 --> 41:25.900
[♪ somber music playing]

41:32.781 --> 41:34.783
[sobbing]

41:39.497 --> 41:41.499
[blood dripping]

42:01.060 --> 42:02.061
[Tommy] Ellie?

42:04.855 --> 42:05.856
Ellie.

42:08.025 --> 42:09.693
Oh. Oh, God.

42:12.238 --> 42:13.239
Hey.

42:19.537 --> 42:21.330
Let's go, come on.
It's okay, it's okay.

42:22.081 --> 42:24.291
Come on. Come on.

42:36.887 --> 42:38.556
[thunder rumbling]

42:38.597 --> 42:41.058
[Dina grunting softly]
Shit.

42:45.104 --> 42:46.438
Oh, thank God.

43:03.747 --> 43:05.749
-[rain pattering]
-[thunder rumbling]

43:12.756 --> 43:14.258
[Tommy]
The park is no go,

43:14.300 --> 43:16.635
so we stick to the south
on our way outta town.

43:17.886 --> 43:20.264
Not a good idea
to move her in this weather,

43:20.306 --> 43:22.349
so pray for sunshine.

43:22.349 --> 43:24.351
Get the horses at first light
and don't look back.

43:24.351 --> 43:25.686
[creaking]

43:42.578 --> 43:43.871
Hey.

43:45.414 --> 43:48.000
You know,
they were part of it, too.

43:50.377 --> 43:51.879
They made their choices.

43:52.630 --> 43:54.048
That's all there is to it.

43:55.758 --> 43:57.635
[thunder rumbling]

44:00.554 --> 44:02.264
But Abby gets to live.

44:03.766 --> 44:04.892
[Tommy] Yeah.

44:05.643 --> 44:07.811
Are you able to make
your peace with that?

44:09.605 --> 44:11.190
Guess I'll have to.

44:15.944 --> 44:18.197
[thunder rumbling softly]

44:24.578 --> 44:26.288
I'm gonna start
packin' the duffels.

44:35.005 --> 44:36.465
[door opens]

44:40.886 --> 44:42.471
[door closes]

44:42.513 --> 44:44.264
Thank you for coming back.

44:47.059 --> 44:49.144
Maybe I didn't want to.

44:50.604 --> 44:52.189
Maybe Tommy made me.

44:53.607 --> 44:54.692
Did he?

44:58.779 --> 45:01.490
[sighs deeply]

45:01.532 --> 45:02.658
Nope.

45:07.871 --> 45:09.832
[softly]
Because you're a good person.

45:13.711 --> 45:14.753
[softly] Yeah.

45:17.339 --> 45:19.341
But also,
the thought did occur...

45:20.634 --> 45:24.430
if I were out there somewhere,
lost and in trouble...

45:26.557 --> 45:28.851
you would set the world
on fire to save me.

45:32.479 --> 45:33.856
I would.

45:38.819 --> 45:41.739
-[clattering]
-[Tommy shouting]

45:43.240 --> 45:46.243
[♪ dramatic music playing]

45:46.785 --> 45:48.787
[both panting]

45:51.665 --> 45:53.125
[gunshot]

45:54.960 --> 45:56.503
-[gasps]
-[door opens]

45:56.545 --> 45:57.880
[Abby] Stand up.

45:59.798 --> 46:01.508
Stand up!

46:01.550 --> 46:03.385
Hands in the air
or I shoot this one too.

46:03.427 --> 46:04.928
-Just run, Ellie!
-Shut the fuck up!

46:04.970 --> 46:06.597
Stop! Stop!

46:06.889 --> 46:07.890
[Tommy groaning]

46:14.938 --> 46:16.940
[thunder rumbling]

46:18.650 --> 46:20.027
You.

46:20.068 --> 46:21.945
Just let him go.

46:24.698 --> 46:26.033
He killed my friends.

46:26.074 --> 46:28.035
No, I did.

46:28.035 --> 46:30.496
I was looking for you.
I didn't mean to hurt them.

46:32.831 --> 46:36.126
I know why you killed Joel.
He did what he did to save me.

46:36.168 --> 46:37.878
I'm the one that you want.

46:39.922 --> 46:41.548
Just let him go.

46:43.509 --> 46:45.219
I let you live.

46:47.513 --> 46:49.598
I let you live.

46:50.057 --> 46:52.059
[panting]

46:52.100 --> 46:53.769
-And you wasted it.
-No, no, no!

46:53.811 --> 46:55.229
[gunshot]

46:55.270 --> 46:57.272
[high-pitched ringing]

47:03.821 --> 47:05.823
[ringing intensifies]

47:07.032 --> 47:09.576
-[ringing stops abruptly]
-[clock ticking]

47:09.618 --> 47:11.078
-[loud banging]
-[Manny] Hey.

47:11.119 --> 47:13.080
-[Abby] Oh, shit.
-You up?

47:13.080 --> 47:15.123
-Well, yeah, now.
-Cool. Alright, come on.

47:15.165 --> 47:16.625
Isaac wants to talk to us.

47:18.168 --> 47:20.921
Okay. Just let me wake up.

47:20.963 --> 47:23.090
-I'll be there in five minutes.
-Alright.

47:23.090 --> 47:24.925
It's your funeral
if you make him wait.

47:24.925 --> 47:26.218
Uh-huh.

47:40.148 --> 47:43.151
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

47:45.320 --> 47:47.322
[dog barking in distance]

47:54.454 --> 47:56.456
[barking continues]

48:00.043 --> 48:03.046
♪♪

48:08.677 --> 48:10.679
[♪ dramatic music swells]

48:23.191 --> 48:25.193
["Burden in My Hand"
by Soundgarden playing}

48:25.235 --> 48:27.821
♪ Follow me into the desert ♪

48:27.863 --> 48:31.533
♪ As thirsty as you are ♪

48:33.493 --> 48:37.706
♪ Crack a smile
and cut your mouth ♪

48:37.748 --> 48:41.960
♪ And drown in alcohol ♪

48:44.296 --> 48:48.717
♪ I shot my love today ♪

48:48.759 --> 48:52.429
♪ Would you cry for me? ♪

48:54.640 --> 48:57.976
♪ I lost my head again ♪

48:59.227 --> 49:02.356
♪ Would you lie for me? ♪

49:04.399 --> 49:10.280
♪ Fear is strong
and love's for everyone ♪

49:10.322 --> 49:13.492
♪ Who isn't me ♪

49:15.535 --> 49:19.039
♪ Kill your health
and kill yourself ♪

49:19.081 --> 49:24.336
♪ And kill everything
you love ♪

49:25.545 --> 49:29.883
♪ And if you live,
you can fall to pieces ♪

49:30.217 --> 49:34.304
♪ And suffer
with my ghost ♪
